Z||000000||RZURCTN||10-04-1999||09:38 PM||||I recently shredded my camshaft timing gear on my little '84 SE. After replacing it with a new one and putting everything back together, the car now refuses to run right.  There is a miss on the No. 3 cylinder.  The spark is good but the ALCL diagnostic tells me a code 42 EST.  I tested all the electrical (ignition coil, pick up coil, ignition module, ect.) and can't figure out why it won't fire!! I am considering replacing the engine entirely at the moment.<p>[This message has been edited by RZURCTN (edited 10-04-1999).]||||reg||8
